---
description: "Vercel deployment standards — applies to the FRONTEND (frontend/) only. The Pericles backend deploys to Coolify."
globs: "frontend/**/*.{ts,js,tsx,jsx,json}"
alwaysApply: false
---

> ## ⚠️ Scope: frontend only
>
> Pericles is **two deploys on two providers**:
>
> | Component | Host |
> |---|---|
> | `frontend/` — Next.js/React | **Vercel** ← this rule applies here |
> | `backend/` — Express + socket.io | **Coolify** (Docker container, port `4112`) |
>
> The serverless-function, cron, and backend-environment sections below are
> **not** how the Pericles backend is deployed. The backend is a long-running
> container: see `.claude/rules/13-infrastructure.md` and `DEPLOYMENT.md`, and
> use the `coolify-deploy` skill to trigger deploys, watch builds, and sync env
> vars.
>
> Note also that `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are inlined into the client bundle at
> build time, so changing one requires a rebuild, not just an env edit.

